# The words of the data feed (SOT-212). Edit the sentences here, not the generated pages.
#
# scripts/data_feed.py reads this file and fills in the $names. A line that starts with "#" before the
# first section is a comment. Sections start with a line like "=== block ===". Write $$ for a literal $.
# Marks ("new since 2610", "changed since 2610", "fixed since 2610") compare with the summary the previous feed
# stored, not with the last published site. After the next feed they are gone: the pages show only what changed
# since the feed before. The first feed has nothing to compare with and marks nothing.
# The generated text must never contain the words the site does not use (see AGENTS.md): the script
# refuses to write a page that does, and the tests check it.
#
# Sections:
#   block    the short section in docs/known-limitations.md (between the data-feed markers)
#   gaps     the whole page docs/data-gaps.md
#   first, first_page  the sentences that stand in, in the block and on the page, until the first summary arrives
#   phrases  one "name = words" line each; small pieces the sections use

=== block ===
## Where the FAA data has gaps

ATC flies the FAA's published data, and the FAA's data has gaps. This section describes FAA cycle $cycle, effective $effective, and was made on $generated. It changes with every cycle.

**Approaches.** The FAA publishes $published instrument approaches in this cycle. $coded_by_faa of them come coded by the FAA, SeventyOneTen built $built_by_us more from the FAA's own approach forms, and $missing are missing, so ATC does not offer those yet.$reasons_intro

$reasons

**Airports.** Of $airports_total airports, $all_available have every approach SeventyOneTen could find. $missing_airports airports are missing at least one approach: $runway_without_approach where a runway has no approach, $circling_only_missing where ATC has no approach at all in its data and only circling approaches are missing, and $some_missing others.$airports_change See [the full lists of airports](data-gaps.md).

**Fix names.** $fixes_confirmed of $fixes_total fix names are confirmed (lexicon version $lexicon_version, $lexicon_generated). ATC says a confirmed fix the way controllers say it and any other fix as it is written.$fixes_change

$what_changed

=== gaps ===
# FAA data gaps: the full lists

These are the airports where the FAA's data has gaps, for FAA cycle $cycle, effective $effective. The lists were made on $generated from the data ATC is using now, and they change with every cycle. The short version is under [Where the FAA data has gaps](known-limitations.md#where-the-faa-data-has-gaps) on the Known limitations page.

$what_changed

## Runways with no approach

At these airports a runway has no instrument approach at all in ATC's data, so ATC cannot clear you for an approach to it. There are $runway_without_approach such airports.

$runway_table

## Airports with only circling approaches missing

At these airports ATC has no approach at all in its data, and the only approaches missing are circling ones. There are $circling_only_missing such airports.

$circling_table

## Other airports missing some approaches

These airports have approaches in ATC's data, but at least one published approach is missing. There are $some_missing such airports.

$some_missing_table
$fixed_section

